<h1>Lilian Jimenez</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 4th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.lilianforstaterep.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (lilianforstaterep.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Her campaign site says she wants to tax corporations and high earners rather than working people, stabilize property taxes, expand community land trusts, protect reproductive rights, and restrict immigration enforcement at schools, courthouses, day cares, universities, and hospitals. In a Sun-Times questionnaire she named ICE enforcement, health care, housing, child care costs, and property taxes as the district&#39;s top concerns.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Immigration and labor attorney who served as chief of staff to Cook County Commissioner Jesus &#39;Chuy&#39; Garcia, director of the Fair Labor Standards Division at the Illinois Department of Labor, and administrator of the Office of Welcoming Centers at the Illinois Department of Human Services.</p>
